  "notes": "Saraiki (سرائیکی) Shahmukhi consonant inventory, extending the Urdu-style Perso-Arabic abjad with four implosive letters (ٻ ɓ, ڄ ʄ, ڏ ɗ, ڳ ɠ) that are the language's most distinctive typological feature (Shackle 1976). Each implosive letter earns its key by test 1: its IPA is not derivable by composing a base letter with a diacritic — it is a dedicated grapheme the Anjuman Taraqqi-e-Saraiki standard assigns no other role. Short vowels are not written (abjad); ا و ی carry long-vowel/glide values only, consistent with the input contract of every other abjad spec in this repository (vowelised or lexicon-backed input is a downstream concern). Saraiki word stress is not orthographically predictable and is exempt per quality_tiers.md. Registered against WikiPron's skr_arab_broad gold.",
